<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sneferu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">26th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/26th-century-bce">26th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sneferu was the founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s Fourth Dynasty, reigning in the 26th century BCE. He built the Bent Pyramid and the Red Pyramid at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dahshur">Dahshur</a> and completed the pyramid at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meidum">Meidum</a>, developing the first true pyramids. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo-stone">Palermo Stone</a> records his expeditions to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> and the arrival of forty ships laden with cedar, probably from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byblos">Byblos</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sneferu.jpg" alt="Sneferu" width="320" height="550" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Mortel · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sneferu_portrait,_Cairo_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
